   "source": "cityspark",
   "source_event_id": "260807Ydo8EYKm9U2dOUqolzU4NQ",
   "title": "13th Annual Trick or Trunk",
   "start": "2026-10-31T15:00:00-06:00",
   "end": "2026-10-31T17:00:00-06:00",
   "all_day": false,
   "timezone": "America/Denver",
   "url": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1583903103521443/",
   "description": "13th Annual Trick or Trunk Put on your favorite costume and join the Dickinson Area Chamber of Commerce for the 13th Annual Trick or Trunk on Saturday, October 31, from 3:00 PM to 5:00 PM in Downtown Legacy Square and the two blocks surrounding City Hall. This free, family-friendly Halloween tradition brings together local businesses, organizations, and the community for an afternoon of trick-or-treating, festive fun, and plenty of candy! Children and families are invited to stroll through downtown, visit participating businesses and decorated trunks, and enjoy a safe and exciting Halloween experience. Event Highlights Trick-or-treating with local businesses and organizations Decorated trunks and festive displays Safe, family-friendly Halloween fun Thousands of pieces of candy for little ghosts and goblins Costumes encouraged for all ages! Best Decorated Trunk/Space Contest Returns! Participating businesses and organizations will once again compete for the title of Best Decorated Trunk/Space. Event attendees will have the opportunity to vote for their favorite display by scanning QR codes located throughout the event. Voting will close at the end of Trick or Trunk, and the winner will be announced on the Dickinson Area Chamber of Commerce's social media following the event. Whether you're a business looking to connect with the community or a family looking to celebrate Halloween, Trick or Trunk is an event you won't want to miss. Event Details Date: Saturday, October 31 Time: 3:00 PM – 5:00 PM Location: Downtown Legacy Square and the two blocks surrounding City Hall \\(same route as last year\\) Admission is free, so gather your family, wear your best costume, and join us for one of Dickinson's favorite Halloween traditions. We can't wait to celebrate with you!",
